{"version":"bsb","book":"job","chapter":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"Job Decries His Comforters"},{"kind":"paragraph","indent":0,"runs":[{"verse":1,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Then Job answered:"}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"“I have heard many things like these;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"miserable comforters are you all."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Is there no end to your long-winded speeches?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"What provokes you to continue testifying?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"I could also speak like you"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"if you were in my place;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"I could heap up words against you"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and shake my head at you."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"But I would encourage you with my mouth,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and the consolation of my lips would bring relief."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":6,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Even if I speak, my pain is not relieved,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":6,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and if I hold back, how will it go away?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":7,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Surely He has now exhausted me;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":7,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"You have devastated all my family."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":8,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"You have bound me, and it has become a witness;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":8,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"my frailty rises up and testifies against me."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":9,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"His anger has torn me and opposed me;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":9,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He gnashes His teeth at me."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":9,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"My adversary pierces me with His eyes."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"They open their mouths against me"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and strike my cheeks with contempt;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":10,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"they join together against me."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":11,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"God has delivered me to unjust men;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":11,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He has thrown me to the clutches of the wicked."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":12,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"I was at ease, but He shattered me;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":12,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He seized me by the neck and crushed me."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":12,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He has set me up as His target;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":13,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"His archers surround me."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":13,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He pierces my kidneys without mercy"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":13,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and spills my gall on the ground."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":14,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"He breaks me with wound upon wound;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":14,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He rushes me like a mighty warrior."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":15,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"I have sewn sackcloth over my skin;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":15,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"I have buried my horn in the dust."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":16,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"My face is red with weeping,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":16,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and deep shadows ring my eyes;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":17,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"yet my hands are free of violence"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":17,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and my prayer is pure."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":18,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"O earth, do not cover my blood;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":18,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"may my cry for help never be laid to rest."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":19,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Even now my witness is in heaven,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":19,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and my advocate is on high."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":20,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"My friends are my scoffers"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":20,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"as my eyes pour out tears to God."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":21,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Oh, that a man might plead with God"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":21,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"as he pleads with his neighbor!"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":22,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"For when only a few years are past"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":22,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"I will go the way of no return.[’’]"}]}]}
